SGF files from [gokifu.com](http://gokifu.com/) use the `AP` property `SGFC:2.0`, and they contain unconventional komi values similar to those found in `foxwq` files.
Examples include:

```cpp
if (komi == 550 || komi == 275)
  komi = 5.5f;
else if (komi == 325 || komi == 650)
  komi = 6.5f;
else if (komi == 375 || komi == 750)
  komi = 7.5f;
else if (komi == 350 || komi == 700)
  komi = 7.0f;
```

In this change, the `SGFC:2.0` tag has been added to the existing property check:

```cpp
if (hasProperty("AP")) {
  auto ap = getProperties("AP");
  if (contains(ap, "foxwq") || contains(ap, "SGFC:2.0"))
```

This update extends the existing komi hack logic to correctly handle `SGFC:2.0` files in addition to `foxwq` sources.

